Line ending error: 'rejects_crlf.jesus' contains CRLF (\r\n) line endings (first CRLF found on line 1).

Jesus only supports LF (\n) line endings.
CRLF line endings (\r\n) are rejected to keep diffs clean and avoid
silent whitespace changes that clutter version control history.

Tip: configure your editor to use 'LF (Unix)' line endings and re-save the file.
In VS Code, click the CRLF/LF indicator in the bottom-right status bar to switch.
